WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.060
[gentle music]

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:06.470
AI computing is pushing
the boundaries of silicon,

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.900
and chiplets are being used
more and more for AI use cases.

4
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.090
But when we break apart
a monolithic system on chip die

5
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.600
into a modularized system
and package of chiplets,

6
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.220
it benefits more than just the AI use case
or whatever the original use case was.

7
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.020
The chiplets from the resulting
disaggregation of a large monolithic

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.870
SoC can end up on a marketplace
where other product teams may

9
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.420
use them for different AI chips,
as well as chips in network switches,

10
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.140
servers, and PCs, as just some examples.

11
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.070
The marketplace of chiplets will
also enable system design variants,

12
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.900
whether for different
requirements or future-proofing.

13
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.100
Let's look at a progression
of possibilities.

14
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.830
A modularized system could
simply resemble the original

15
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.840
monolithic SoC in the case
of a baseline architectural conversion.

16
00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.890
Creating a variant may
involve swapping out a logic

17
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.600
chip for a more programmable FPGA.

18
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.170
And taking things a step
further, we could add a sea

19
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.440
of cores inference engine
and some Ethernet connectivity.

20
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.510
And finally, we can imagine a future
variant of that step with some

21
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.260
upgraded accelerator
and upgraded Ethernet networking.

22
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.820
While only an example,

23
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.390
those variants would be impossibly
cost-prohibitive using monolithic designs,

24
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.880
but the flexibility enabled with chiplets
opens a world of possibilities.

25
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.660
[gentle music]

